External programs, invoked and never linked
-------------------------------------------

TianWen can drive several third-party programs as separate processes, passing data
through files and reading their output back. None of their code is compiled into
or distributed with TianWen, and each is obtained and licensed by the user
directly from its author:

  ASTAP (`AstapPlateSolver`)                 https://www.hnsky.org/astap.htm
  astrometry.net (`AstrometryNetPlateSolver`) https://astrometry.net
  GraXpert (gradient correction)             https://graxpert.com
  RC-Astro BlurXTerminator / NoiseXTerminator / StarXTerminator  https://www.rc-astro.com
  SETI Astro Suite ONNX models               https://www.setiastro.com

**Driving these programs to process images is ordinary licensed use and is not
restricted here.** RC-Astro runs as a separate process (`rc-astro --json`) against
the user's own licence, and SETI Astro's ONNX models are fetched by the user with
`tools/tianwen-ai-models-fetch.ps1`. TianWen distributes **no third-party model
weights** and no vendor binaries of its own; it locates what the user installed.
Nothing in this section forms part of TianWen's Corresponding Source, because none
of it is part of TianWen.

The one restriction is narrow and applies only to building our own models:
RC-Astro's licence forbids using its outputs to create, train, validate or
benchmark a competing model, naming paired input/output datasets explicitly. So
TianWen's own model work (docs/plans/ai-denoise-deconv.md) uses no RC-Astro or
SETI Astro output anywhere in its training, validation or metric path, and SETI
Astro is excluded on the same assumption pending verification of its terms. That
prohibition is contractual rather than a matter of copyright, so TianWen's own
licence has no bearing on it either way.
